 "source": "Eastman Kodak Company, KODAK PLUS-X Pan and PLUS-X Pan Professional Films, KODAK Publication No. F-8 (September 1997, minor revision 9-97); curves read from the PDF's vector chart paths (page 8)",
 "notes": "Approximate digitization; not supplied or endorsed by Eastman Kodak Company. The page-8 characteristic curves are vector paths in the PDF; curve vertices were read directly from the path geometry (no raster tracing) and axes calibrated on the vector frame and tick marks (log H -3.0..+1.0, density 0..4.0), then resampled linearly on a 0.02 log H grid. Data are for KODAK PLUS-X Pan Film / PX (135 and 35 mm long rolls), the product named on page 8. The same publication also charts PLUS-X Pan Professional PXP (page 10, HC-110 5/8/12/16 min) and PXE/PXT (page 11, HC-110 3/6/9/15 min); those are different products and are not included. Characteristic curves (page 8, 'Exposure: Daylight, 1/25 second; Densitometry: Diffuse visual'): two charts, KODAK HC-110 (Dilution B) 68 F large tank 5/8/12/16 min, and KODAK T-MAX Developer 75 F small tank 5/7/9/11 min; all eight are in all_curves. Curves were matched to their time labels by density order at log H -1.0 (longer time, higher density). channels.k is T-MAX Developer 75 F small tank 5 min: the manual-processing starting points (page 3) are 'intended to produce a contrast index of 0.56', and the PX/PXP small-tank table gives T-MAX Developer at 75 F for 5 min, which is the only charted curve that equals a recommended starting-point time and temperature (the HC-110 large-tank starting point at 68 F is 5 1/2 min, between the charted 5 and 8 min). The T-MAX chart curves begin at the chart's left frame (log H -3.0) and may be clipped there; the HC-110 curves begin at log H -2.87. x is log H (lux-seconds) as charted. log_h_ref: none. The charts carry no 18% grey, speed-point or normal-exposure mark, so no reference exposure is placed; the text gives ISO 125/22. spectral_sensitivity: not present. This datasheet (KODAK Publication F-8) publishes no spectral sensitivity curve, so the field is omitted rather than invented. rms_granularity is the printed diffuse rms granularity 10 for PX/PXP ('Extremely Fine'; net diffuse density 1.0, 48 um aperture, 12x; HC-110 Dil B 70 F 5 min large tank, contrast index 0.56); PXE/PXT is 14. No granularity curve is published. Not recorded (no field in this schema): contrast-index vs development-time curves, MTF curve (page 9), reciprocity and push-processing tables. Spectral sensitivity is not published in this datasheet; the model uses the KODAK DOUBLE-X 5222 spectral sensitivity as a stand-in (spectral_fallback), not Plus-X data.",
